      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Dynamical mean-field theory made strongly correlated electrons quantitatively tractable and became a central conceptual and computational framework for materials physics.",
        "attribution": "Georges and Kotliar established the modern practical formulation, while Vollhardt was essential to the infinite-dimensional mean-field construction.",
        "maturity": "Its predictions, extensions, and combination with electronic-structure methods are thoroughly established.",
