      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "The jamming framework exposed a unifying transition governing rigidity and disorder in granular matter, foams, colloids, and model amorphous solids.",
        "attribution": "Liu and Nagel articulated the broad organizing idea, and O'Hern helped establish its sharp numerical critical phenomenology.",
        "maturity": "A substantial experimental and theoretical literature supports the central phenomenology and its broad relevance.",
        "uncertainties": [
